From: Ayman <ayman@aymanrgab.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Jun 2026 22:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] media: i2c: ov13b10: Retry clock enable and set rate on
 power_on

The CAMCC MCLK0 branch clock's hardware state can be corrupted after a
camss module reload cycle, causing clk_prepare_enable to return -EBUSY.
Add a retry loop with a delay. Do not call clk_disable_unprepare on
-EBUSY -- the CCF already unprepares internally on failure.

Also call clk_set_rate() to ensure the MCLK0 RCG divider is configured
for 19.2MHz after a power domain cycle.

Signed-off-by: Ayman <ayman@aymanrgab.com>

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov13b10.c
@@ -1223,6 +1223,7 @@
 	struct v4l2_subdev *sd = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	struct ov13b10 *ov13b10 = to_ov13b10(sd);
 	int ret;
+	int retries;
 
 	/* #region debug-point ov13b10-power */
 	dev_dbg(dev,
@@ -1230,7 +1231,18 @@
 		 !IS_ERR_OR_NULL(ov13b10->reset), !!ov13b10->avdd,
 		 !!ov13b10->dvdd, !!ov13b10->dovdd);
 	/* #endregion debug-point ov13b10-power */
-	ret = clk_prepare_enable(ov13b10->img_clk);
+	ret = clk_set_rate(ov13b10->img_clk, OV13B10_EXT_CLK);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		dev_warn(dev, "Failed to set MCLK rate to 19.2MHz: %d\n", ret);
+
+	for (retries = 3; retries > 0; retries--) {
+		ret = clk_prepare_enable(ov13b10->img_clk);
+		if (ret != -EBUSY)
+			break;
+		dev_dbg(dev, "ov13b10-debug: power_on clock busy, retrying...\n");
+		usleep_range(5000, 10000);
+	}
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(dev, "failed to enable imaging clock: %d", ret);
 		return ret;
